# Interpreter-throw closure item 6, the dynamically selected callable: a walked callee selected through the formal
# faults in the walker (12 / 0) and its NATIVE caller -- kept native by its C-door call -- catches interpreter
# (item 2's route, through the formal).  Exit 7.
fn: bad (int: n) int
    return: 12 / n

fn: apply (op(fn: (int: n) int) int(value)) int
    int: native_probe c.abs(value)
    int: got 0
    ---
        got: op(value)
    ---
    catch: interpreter ()
        got: 7
return: got

int: r apply(bad 0)
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: r; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
